    {
      "id": "nNUk7ixR1UAj9aQVsppT7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1810.9844824194897,
      "y": -1469.9875680555388,
      "width": 1656.63916015625,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#6741d9",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "7LOYqQ3GlYuGjbJKAB7bC",
      "index": "a8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1428723053,
      "version": 696,
      "versionNonce": 1305368205,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784652148644,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "As of Apr 2026 ... Jul 2026 (as of writing), the Meta/GCP team took a pause supporting torch_xla and focused on native TPU integrations rather than a JAX wrapper\n    - helpful insight for me to focus on openxla at lower absstractions to limit changes\n    - waiting for official TorchTPU integrations ... could I already do this on google TPU via google colab/kaggle?\n    = python and JAX ... learn more about C++ to support compiler and openxla specifically\n    ? stableHLO",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "As of Apr 2026 ... Jul 2026 (as of writing), the Meta/GCP team took a pause supporting torch_xla and focused on native TPU integrations rather than a JAX wrapper\n    - helpful insight for me to focus on openxla at lower absstractions to limit changes\n    - waiting for official TorchTPU integrations ... could I already do this on google TPU via google colab/kaggle?\n    = python and JAX ... learn more about C++ to support compiler and openxla specifically\n    ? stableHLO",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "iasiPaQQ7S44G9DV28fmS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2421.493375437065,
      "y": -651.9178621431547,
      "width": 2254.149172654182,
      "height": 964.0874565972223,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "7LOYqQ3GlYuGjbJKAB7bC",
      "index": "a9",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1336762317,
      "version": 686,
      "versionNonce": 2110907587,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784652148644,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The TPU Workflow: Data cleaning is done before reaching the\nTPU using CPU frameworks (like Apache Beam, Spark, or Ray) or\nGPUs (via cuDF). \n\nOnce the data is entirely numerical, it is fed onto the TPU as\nraw tensors (using JAX, TensorFlow, or PyTorch). \n\n[1 (https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/pandas-dataframe-tutorial-\nbeginners-guide-to-gpu-accelerated-dataframes-in-python/), \n2 (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ocql-0B4o5c), \n3 (https://code-b.dev/blog/data-processing-machine-learning)]",
      "fontSize": 70.11545138888889,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The TPU Workflow: Data cleaning is done before reaching the TPU using CPU frameworks (like Apache Beam, Spark, or Ray) or GPUs (via cuDF). \n\nOnce the data is entirely numerical, it is fed onto the TPU as raw tensors (using JAX, TensorFlow, or PyTorch). \n\n[1 (https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/pandas-dataframe-tutorial-beginners-guide-to-gpu-accelerated-dataframes-in-python/), \n2 (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ocql-0B4o5c), \n3 (https://code-b.dev/blog/data-processing-machine-learning)]",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
