    {
      "id": "LwbbWsEDPhgQeChzDeDit",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2210.7245445452118,
      "y": 3795.254351281781,
      "width": 1572.3596102043412,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "-VSGKaB19jyqxNWYubFop",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 356945171,
      "version": 423,
      "versionNonce": 39822007,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784659892119,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- NVIDIA CUDA C++ Programming Guide (docs.nvidia.com/cuda) — the canonical reference for the CUDA execution and memory model.\n- NVIDIA Developer Blog (developer.nvidia.com/blog) — practical posts on kernel optimization, Nsight profiling workflows, and mixed-precision training.\n- \"Programming Massively Parallel Processors\" by Kirk & Hwu — the standard GPU-programming textbook, used in many university parallel-computing courses.\n- Google Cloud TPU documentation (cloud.google.com/tpu/docs) — system architecture, performance guide, and profiling guide; complements the TPU papers\nalready logged in the GPU/TPU frame.\n- PyTorch/XLA documentation and GitHub (github.com/pytorch/xla) — official docs for running PyTorch on TPU, including debugging and profiling guides.\n- Horace He, \"Making Deep Learning Go Brrrr From First Principles\" — widely cited practical treatment of compute-bound vs. memory-bound vs. overhead-bound\nperformance analysis.\n- Megatron-LM paper (Shoeybi et al., 2019) — canonical reference for tensor-parallel + pipeline-parallel training at scale.\n- ZeRO / DeepSpeed paper (Rajbhandari et al., 2020) — canonical reference for optimizer-state, gradient, and parameter sharding across data-parallel workers.\n- NVIDIA Nsight Systems & Nsight Compute documentation — official profiling-tool docs, the CUDA-side counterpart to XProf already listed for TPU.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- NVIDIA CUDA C++ Programming Guide (docs.nvidia.com/cuda) — the canonical reference for the CUDA execution and memory model.\n- NVIDIA Developer Blog (developer.nvidia.com/blog) — practical posts on kernel optimization, Nsight profiling workflows, and mixed-precision training.\n- \"Programming Massively Parallel Processors\" by Kirk & Hwu — the standard GPU-programming textbook, used in many university parallel-computing courses.\n- Google Cloud TPU documentation (cloud.google.com/tpu/docs) — system architecture, performance guide, and profiling guide; complements the TPU papers already logged in the GPU/TPU frame.\n- PyTorch/XLA documentation and GitHub (github.com/pytorch/xla) — official docs for running PyTorch on TPU, including debugging and profiling guides.\n- Horace He, \"Making Deep Learning Go Brrrr From First Principles\" — widely cited practical treatment of compute-bound vs. memory-bound vs. overhead-bound performance analysis.\n- Megatron-LM paper (Shoeybi et al., 2019) — canonical reference for tensor-parallel + pipeline-parallel training at scale.\n- ZeRO / DeepSpeed paper (Rajbhandari et al., 2020) — canonical reference for optimizer-state, gradient, and parameter sharding across data-parallel workers.\n- NVIDIA Nsight Systems & Nsight Compute documentation — official profiling-tool docs, the CUDA-side counterpart to XProf already listed for TPU.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "aS"
    },
